Crypto is going through its own disinflation and hardly anyone is talking about it.

New token supply peaked at 26.5% a year in Dec 2021. Today it's 3.3%, the lowest in my data.

Prices haven't responded yet.

Disinflationary regimes are generally good for asset prices, associated with rising productivity and economic growth. In the US, after inflation peaked in 1980 the S&P went sideways for 2 years... then did 13x. Not a perfect analogy, but food for thought.

